title: 'C4''a: local tool tiers (graded probe, tiers 0-3, a live human tier change)'
summary: |-
  Arky designed C4' (TD-2026-10-27-833). The founder's answers changed two parts of the design: tier 3 offers FULL schemas for every tool, and a human raise or lower applies live after a confirm. A builder built C4'a in a worktree (6dc192de..768224e8):
  - tool-tier.ts and a per-model store, with effective tier = min(human ?? skill, window);
  - probe T2-T4 and fingerprintOf;
  - full form in the capability index (fullOfferable, reassembleFull, tokenShape);
  - a tier-aware selector (K 0/4/12/12, slot 0/10%/15%/25%);
  - request.session.tier, a two-phase preview/commit with a single-use 60 s token, human-only;
  - tools_set{surface} with the ack-gated switch;
  - the contracts trigger 'tier'.

  Aegis found no High. M1: unchecked server text in full schemas (required, pattern). Three Lows: the surface change lost on a later reselect, a commit race, and the directory mode. All fixed and re-checked, then the remaining Low was closed: tekken, fullwidth and describe() token shapes. The work was merged into feat/gnomon and pushed (af532886). tsc is clean. The full suite ran 4141 passed and 1 failed: a load timeout in always-edit-scopes, which passes on its own.
