    decision: Tier 3 offers every tool in its full original schema (K 12, slot min(4000, 25%)); tiers 0-2 stay compact
    rationale: 'Founder: full schemas for all'
  - id: c4-live-raise
    decision: A human tier change applies live after a kernel-enforced preview/commit; the old set stays callable until tools_applied
    rationale: 'Founder: right away, but the user confirms what will happen'
  - id: c4-human-replaces
    decision: effective = min(human ?? skill, window), so a human can lower a tier as well as raise it
    rationale: max() would block lowering; lowering is the safer direction
learnings:
  - The neutraliser for tool results must stay narrow (code like `a << 2` or </div>), but third-party schema text needs a broader refuse-shape check. These are two separate lists on purpose.
  - Run the workspace build before `npm run embed`. Embedding against a stale contracts build changes the bundle hash.
